<title>GERMANY: East German Aug industrial orders fall 3.6 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>East German Aug industrial orders fall 3.6 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Aug 96     Jul 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -3.6	 -5.0	+21.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year			-4.9	+19.6	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		133.6	138.6	140.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Aug 96    Jul 96  Aug 96 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     +2.8	-11.5     154.1</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Jul/Aug 96 with May/Jun 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  -4.5</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Jul/Aug 96 with Jul/Aug 95:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +6.8</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +7.5</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +3.7</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +11.2</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -0.9</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   +12.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
